    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d969">

                <pb facs="0985" n="973" xml:id="pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9450: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-30T13:00:00+01:00">March 30, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>277. My 275.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d969-f1"/> With regard to Prince Paul’s
                    meeting with Hitler at Berchtesgaden on March 4 or 5 (not 11) I am informed by
                    reliable source that Hitler said to Prince during 2-hour interview Yugoslavia
                    must sign Tripartite Pact in own interest as in June or July he was going to
                    attack Russia.</p>
                <p>British Minister says foregoing fits in with information he has.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
